"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Favorable findings include a negative surgical margin (0.0), no seminal vesicle invasion (0.0), and absence of lymphovascular invasion. The surgical pathology showed a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) and pathological T2 stage with no extraprostatic extension. Countervailing factors include the preoperative PSA of 8.4 and the finding of Gleason 3+4 on biopsy, which is higher than the initial biopsy grade of 0+0. Furthermore, the absence of lymph node removal means nodal status is unknown, which widens uncertainty. The biopsy-to-prostatectomy difference is noted, with the final pathology reflecting a higher grade. Postoperative PSA and its trajectory are critical unknowns that would significantly revise this prognosis. Missing nodal sampling further complicates the assessment of local control. The fixed estimated horizon is 88.57 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 57.57–119.57 months; its coverage has not been validated."
